<emu-clause id="WebAssembly.compile" spec-type="js api">
  <h1>WebAssembly.compile (_buffer_)</h1>
  <emu-alg>
    1. Let _stableBytes_ be GetBufferSourceCopy(_buffer_).
    1. Return AsynchronouslyCompileWebAssemblyModule(_stableBytes_).
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="AsynchronouslyCompileWebAssemblyModule" spec-type="js api" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>AsynchronouslyCompileWebAssemblyModule(
    _bytes_: a List of byte values,
  ) </h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Let _promise_ be ? CreateNewPromise().
  1. Let _module_ be CompileWebAssemblyModule(_bytes_).
  1. If _module_ is an error, perform RejectPromise(_promise_, a newly created *CompileError* object).
  1. Else,
    1. Let _moduleObject_ be ConstructWebAssemblyModule(_module_, _bytes_).
    1. Perform ResolvePromise(_promise_, _moduleObject_).
  1. Return _promise_.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="CompileWebAssemblyModule" spec-type="js api" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>CompileWebAssemblyModule(
    _bytes_: a List of byte values,
  ) </h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Let _module_ be WASM/moduledecode(_bytes_).
  1. If _module_ is an error, return _module_.
  1. Let _res_ be WASM/modulevalidate(_module_).
  1. If _res_ is an error, return _res_.
  1. Return _module_.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="ConstructWebAssemblyModule" spec-type="js api" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>ConstructWebAssemblyModule(_module_, _bytes_)</h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Let _moduleObject_ be a new newly created Module object.
  1. Set _moduleObject_.[[Module]] to _module_.
  1. Set _moduleObject_.[[Bytes]] to _bytes_.
  1. Return _moduleObject_.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="GetBufferSourceCopy" spec-type="web idl" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>GetBufferSourceCopy (
    _jsBufferSource_: an ArrayBuffer, a SharedArrayBuffer, a DataView, or a TypedArray,
  ): a List of byte values</h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Let _jsArrayBuffer_ be _jsBufferSource_.
  1. Let _offset_ be 0.
  1. Let _length_ be 0.
  1. If _jsBufferSource_ has a [[ViewedArrayBuffer]] internal slot, then
    1. Set _jsArrayBuffer_ to _jsBufferSource_.[[ViewedArrayBuffer]].
    1. Set _offset_ to _jsBufferSource_.[[ByteOffset]].
    1. Set _length_ to _jsBufferSource_.[[ByteLength]].
  1. Otherwise,
    1. Assert: _jsBufferSource_ is an ArrayBuffer or SharedArrayBuffer.
    1. Set _length_ to _jsBufferSource_.[[ArrayBufferByteLength]].
  1. If IsDetachedBuffer(_jsArrayBuffer_) is *true*, then return a new empty List.
  1. Let _bytes_ be a new empty List.
  1. For each integer _i_ such that 0 ≤ _i_ ≤ _length_ - 1, in ascending order, do
    1. Append GetValueFromBuffer(_jsArrayBuffer_, _i_ + _offset_, ~uint8~, *true*, ~unordered~) to _bytes_.
  1. Return _bytes_.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="CreateNewPromise" spec-type="web idl" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>CreateNewPromise (): either a normal completion containing a PromiseCapability Record or a throw completion </h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Let _constructor_ be %Promise%.
  1. Return ? NewPromiseCapability(_constructor_).
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="ResolvePromise" spec-type="web idl" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>ResolvePromise(_p_, _x_)</h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Perform ! Call(_p_.[[Resolve]], *undefined*, « _x_ »).
  1. Return ~unused~.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="RejectPromise" spec-type="web idl" type="abstract operation">
  <h1>RejectPromise(_p_, _x_)</h1>
  <emu-alg>
  1. Perform ! Call(_p_.[[Reject]], *undefined*, « _x_ »).
  1. Return ~unused~.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>
